-- R31 - THEMATIC HOLD AND BOOK BRAKE, second draft: supersedes R30 before it goes in force. Same tenor and brake;
-- part 2 changed from a 10-session lock on view closes to a view change allowed at any time with a stated new reason.
-- Source: thread "Sharpen trading approach for January restart", 21 Nov 2026 16:46 SGT, the owner: "if u have a
-- really compelling reason to change view then it shd be explained and can be done".
-- Proposed 21 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R31".
-- dash.decide_rules then marks R30 superseded by R31. The call below is the exact call that was run.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R31' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Thematic cards are 1-to-3-month expressions on wider stops; a view change closes a card at any time only with a stated new reason; a book-level drawdown brake halves then stops new cards", "body": "THEMATIC HOLD AND BOOK BRAKE (owner's go-ahead of 21 Nov 2026, thread \"Sharpen trading approach for January restart\": he will follow the books with real money from January 2027 and left trade choice and tenor to the runs; December is the paper trial). Three parts. Tactical cards are unchanged. Replaces R30 before it goes in force (owner, 21 Nov 16:46 SGT: \"if u have a really compelling reason to change view then it shd be explained and can be done\").\n\n1. THEMATIC TENOR. A new THEMATIC card is expressed for a planned hold of 15 to 60 sessions. Its carded structure has a tenor of at least one month that covers the planned hold: an option or spread with premium = 1R (R01), or a forward or future rolled under R07; for a cash FX thematic card this replaces R07's usual 2-week tenor with an outright forward covering the planned hold, R07's carry and roll mechanics unchanged. A 1-week or 2-week structure is not a thematic expression; a view whose catalyst lands inside five sessions is carded as TACTICAL or not at all. A linear thematic stop sits beyond the wider of 2 ATR(20) daily and the named structural level; r/r and EV are computed on that stop. The card prints \"HOLD <planned sessions> · tenor <expiry or roll date>\" after the TREND line.\n\n2. VIEW CHANGE BY REASON. A thematic card may close on a changed view at any time, including its first 10 sessions, when the run prints \"VIEW CHANGED: <what is new> · <source, date> · <why it breaks the thesis or its catalyst>\". What is new must be information not in the card's inputs at entry (a dated release, decision, flow or positioning datum, or a signpost met); a price move toward the stop, a lower mark or a contrary voice alone is not a reason and is printed as evidence. R08's review-first step still runs.\n\n3. BOOK BRAKE, printed in the BOOK CHECK from the SCORECARD's cum R and peak (per-unit R). Drawdown from peak of 5R or more: every new card is size 0.5 (META size), whatever its tier. 8R or more: no new cards except HEDGE cards for 5 sessions, then size 0.5 until the book recovers half the drawdown. Print \"BRAKE: off\" or \"BRAKE: half size (DD <x>R)\" or \"BRAKE: no new cards until <date> (DD <x>R)\". The brake never closes an open card.\n\nScoring: the weekly review cuts thematic cards opened from 23 Nov 2026 by hold bucket (0-5, 6-10, 11+ sessions) and exit type beside the earlier cards, and scores each VIEW CHANGED close against the R the card would have had at its stop or target. Interim read for the owner on 8 Jan 2027, before his first real trades; decision at 20 closed thematic cards under this rule or 28 Feb 2027.", "rationale": "On 21 Nov 2026 the owner said he will follow the Takeaways trades rigorously from January 2027 and left the choice of trades and tenor to the runs. The Fable book's own record says its losses sit in thematic cards that lived five sessions or less (stopped on tight stops or closed on a changed view) while thematic cards held 11 sessions or more made most of its R, and tactical washout cards were net positive. The AI-unwind theme was on the book for weeks but carded as 1-to-2-week structures that monetised little. So the thematic expression is lengthened and its stop widened, tactical cards stay as they are, and a book brake is added because real money will follow the book. The owner then objected to a 10-session lock on view closes. The record agrees with him: early view closes on thematic cards lost little each, less than a stop would have cost, and the losses sat in tight stops. So a view change stays allowed at any time, but only with a stated new reason, and each one is scored against holding.", "evidence": "dash.trades model fable, 37 closed cards to 21 Nov 2026, cut by tclass x hold (filled to closed) x exit status; dash.book_state fable SCORECARD (cum R, peak, max DD, view-changed closes). Figures are kept out of the public repo.", "revert_if": "Revert if 5 thematic cards opened under this rule stop out in a row, if thematic cards opened under it lose more R in their first 10 sessions than the earlier thematic cards did over the same window by the 8 Jan read, or if a VIEW CHANGED close prints no new dated reason on 2 or more days.", "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread", "supersedes": "R30"}$j$::jsonb);
